      "side": 1,
      "message": "from a code perspective it is pretty clear: TYPE_UNKNOWN is when you cannot answer the question \"what type\", TYPE_UNSPECIFIED is when the type is not defined by the specs.\n\nfrom a public api perspective, there is actually no way to observe TYPE_UNKNOWN, because it is only produced by the @hide static method macAddressType when the argument is invalid (instead of throwing). Typically the result of that function is going to be used in a switch, so it is fine to not throw I think.\n\nSo I am going to hide TYPE_UNKNOWN and map it to -1, and the renumber TYPE_UNSPECIFIED to 0, which is a bit more logical.",
      "parentUuid": "f4255d5a_7616af88",
